note as N1
  Font loading
  - The default font is loaded from the project assets folder: DEFAULT_FONT_PATH (adjust to the real file name in /assets/fonts).
    It is embedded with include_bytes! in release builds so the executable is self-contained.
  - The font is rasterised by fontdue at the pixel height that makes the glyph box fit cell_w x cell_h (8 x 15).
    mask(ch) returns an alpha mask of EXACTLY cell_w * cell_h bytes: the glyph is placed on the baseline, clipped to the cell.
  - If the font has no glyph for ch, mask() returns the mask of '?' and contains() returns false.
  - If the asset is a BITMAP font (BDF / PSF) replace TtfGlyphSource by another GlyphSource implementation;
    nothing else in the design changes (everything depends on the GlyphSource trait only).
end note

note as N2
  render() - exact compositing (see activity diagram 20a). The input is the FLATTENED frame (Compositor::flatten): hidden layers are already left out,
  glyph / ink colour / fill colour are already mixed across the layers.
  - Output size = canvas.pixel_width x canvas.pixel_height (1920 x 1080 for the default canvas), RGBA8, alpha always 255.
  - pixel = flat.background; if cell.fill.a > 0 pixel = cell.fill.over(pixel) (opaque result);
    then for each glyph pixel: a = div255(mask_alpha * cell.ink.a); pixel = lerp(pixel, cell.ink.rgb, a / 255).
  ThumbnailBuilder::build(flat): ONE pixel per cell (cols x rows image):
    base = flat.page_color(c);  if glyph != ' ' pixel = lerp(base, cell.ink.rgb, 0.6 * cell.ink.a / 255) else pixel = base.
  Callers flatten first: the canvas renderer and the thumbnail cache cache the FlatFrame per Frame.revision, exports flatten once per frame.
end note

note as N3
  wrap(kind, payload): header.magic = kind.magic(), version = 1, uncompressed_len = payload.len(), crc32 = crc32fast(payload),
  payload is compressed with zstd level 3 and flags bit0 = 1 (stored_len = compressed length).
  If compression does not make it smaller, store raw with flags bit0 = 0 (stored_len = uncompressed_len).
  A payload larger than 512 MiB is refused with FormatError::TooLarge (the same limit unwrap() enforces), so a file that was written can always be read back.
  unwrap(kind, bytes): see decode activity diagram (20b). Binary layouts: diagram 08.
  Which codec writes what: .aspr = layered frames (every layer, both planes, layer name / visibility / opacity); .ascii and .aanim = FLATTENED frames.
end note

note as N4
  save(path, project): bytes = AsprCodec.encode(project); AtomicWriter::write(path, bytes).
  load(path): read whole file -> AsprCodec.decode. io NotFound -> RepoError::NotFound.
  The caller (AsciiPaintApp) is responsible for project.touch_modified(now) before save and for history.mark_clean() after success.
end note

note as N5
  write(path, bytes): 1) tmp = path + ".tmp" in the same directory  2) write all bytes, flush, File::sync_all()
  3) fs::rename(tmp, path) (atomic replace on the same volume)  4) on ANY error remove tmp and return the error.
  A crash therefore leaves either the old file or the new file, never a half-written one.
end note

note as N6
  - Stored as JSON { "version": 1, "entries": [ {"name", "path", "last_opened_unix"} ] } in <config_dir>/AsciiPaint/recent.json
    (dirs::config_dir()). Missing / corrupt file -> empty list (a corrupt file is renamed recent.json.bad, never a crash).
  - touch(): remove an existing entry with the same path, insert at index 0, truncate to MAX_ENTRIES, persist().
  - entries() is always sorted by last_opened_unix descending (guaranteed by touch()).
  - Called on: project created, project opened, Save As to a new .aspr path.
end note

note as N7
  PNG       : flat = Compositor::flatten(selected frame); buf = FrameRasterizer::render(&flat); image crate encodes RGBA8 PNG; AtomicWriter.
  .ascii    : AsciiCodec.encode(AsciiImage{ canvas, font_name, frame = flat of the selected frame }); AtomicWriter. ONE flattened image, no layers.
  .aanim    : AanimCodec.encode(AsciiAnimation{ canvas, font_name, fps, looping, frames = every frame flattened }); AtomicWriter.
  ASCII sequence : start_ascii_sequence() clones the frames into an AsciiSequenceWorker and spawns ONE std::thread; returns immediately.
  MP4       : start_mp4() clones the frames into Mp4Worker and spawns ONE std::thread; returns immediately.
  PNG / .ascii / .aanim run synchronously on the UI thread (small, fast). The sequence and the MP4 are asynchronous (at most ONE job at a time).
  Hidden layers are never exported. Only .aspr keeps the layers.
end note

note as N8
  Mp4Worker.run():
  1. spawn  ffmpeg -y -hide_banner -loglevel error -f rawvideo -pix_fmt rgba -s {W}x{H} -framerate {fps} -i pipe:0
            -vf pad=ceil(iw/2)*2:ceil(ih/2)*2 -c:v libx264 -preset medium -crf 18 -pix_fmt yuv420p -movflags +faststart
            -f mp4 {out}.part      (stdin piped, stderr piped; no shell is used, each token is one argument)
  2. a helper thread drains stderr into a ring buffer of the last 4 KiB (prevents a full pipe from blocking ffmpeg).
  3. for i in 0..frames.len(): if cancel is set -> kill child, delete {out}.part, send Cancelled, return.
       flat = Compositor::flatten(frames[i]); buf = FrameRasterizer::render(&flat); stdin.write_all(&buf.pixels); send Progress(i + 1, total).
  4. drop(stdin); status = child.wait(). status != 0 -> delete .part, send Failed(FfmpegFailed(code, stderr_tail)).
  5. fs::rename({out}.part, {out}); send Finished(out).
  Any io error on the pipe -> kill child, delete .part, send Failed(Io).
end note

note as N9
  find(): 1) <exe dir>/ffmpeg(.exe)  2) search every directory in PATH for ffmpeg(.exe).  Returns the first executable found.
  Evaluated once at startup and again each time the Save modal opens (so installing ffmpeg does not need a restart).
end note

note as N10
  AsciiSequenceWorker.run()  (one .ascii file per frame, same flattened format as the single-frame export)
  names = SequenceNamer::names(base, count) = "<base>_frame<NNN>.ascii", NNN = 1-based index zero-padded to max(3, digits(count)).
  1. for i in 0..frames.len(): if cancel is set -> delete every {folder}/{name}.part written so far, send Cancelled, return.
       flat = Compositor::flatten(frames[i]); bytes = AsciiCodec.encode(AsciiImage{ canvas, font_name, frame: flat });
       write bytes to {folder}/{names[i]}.part (flush + sync_all); send Progress(i + 1, total).
  2. after the LAST frame: rename every .part to its final name (fast; an existing file with that name is replaced).
  3. send Finished(folder). Any io / format error in step 1 -> delete all .part files written so far, send Failed(..).
  Because the final names appear only in step 2, a cancelled export or an encode / write error never leaves a half-written sequence and never destroys older files.
  A failure INSIDE step 2 (e.g. a locked file) deletes the remaining .part files and reports the file name; names already renamed stay.
end note

note as N11
  BrushStore - the user's brush library, stored as JSON { "version": 1, "brushes": [ BrushRecord ] } in <config_dir>/AsciiPaint/brushes.json.
  - Only CUSTOM brushes are stored (BrushRecord.cells: row-major, null = empty stamp cell, otherwise a one-character string).
    Built-in brushes come from BrushLibrary::with_builtins() and are never written.
  - open_default(): missing file -> built-ins only. Corrupt file or a record that fails Brush::validate -> the file is renamed brushes.json.bad
    and the library starts with the built-ins (never a crash). Valid records are kept when only some records are bad.
  - upsert(b): BrushLibrary::upsert (validates, assigns the id), then persist() with AtomicWriter. remove(id): BrushLibrary::remove, then persist().
    If persist() fails the in-memory change stays for this run and the caller shows an ErrorModal.
end note

note as N12
  ImportService::load(path)
  - The extension (case-insensitive) decides: "txt" -> TextImporter::parse, "ascii" -> AsciiCodec.decode. Anything else -> UnsupportedType.
  - A file larger than MAX_FILE_BYTES -> TooLarge. Missing file -> NotFound. Other read errors -> Io.
  - PlainText: ParsedText (rules in activity diagram 20d). width = longest line, height = number of lines. No characters at all -> Empty.
    Text up to 4096 x 4096 is accepted: the project can only grow to 1024 x 1024, anything larger is cut off (the import modal says how much).
  - AsciiImage: width = canvas.cols, height = canvas.rows of the file. The file's frame background colour and font name are ignored.
  - ImportedFile.name = file name without extension, cut to 64 chars (used as the new layer name).
  - to_buffer(ink): origin (0, 0), mask all true.
      PlainText : every character except ' ' -> InkCell{ glyph, color: ink }, spaces -> InkCell::EMPTY, fill = TRANSPARENT.
      AsciiImage: InkCell{ glyph, color: the file's ink colour } (blank glyph -> EMPTY), fill = the file's fill colour; `ink` is ignored.
  - warnings (shown in the import modal): replaced invalid UTF-8 sequences, expanded tabs.
end note

